---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbj/asbj22.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Defining Control — the Basis for Consolidation" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Uniform Accounting Policies Within the Group" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Elimination of Intercompany Transactions and Balances" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Non-Controlling Interests Presentation" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Fiscal Year-End Alignment — a Practical J-GAAP-Specific Rule" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Consolidating a Subsidiary at Acquisition" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Fiscal Year-End Misalignment" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
<div class="section-header" id="s1">
  <span class="num">1</span>
  <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card ci span2">
    <div class="ctitle ci">Presenting a group as a single economic entity</div>
    <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 22 establishes the FRAMEWORK for CONSOLIDATED financial statements — presenting a PARENT company and its SUBSIDIARIES as a SINGLE economic reporting entity, rather than as a collection of legally SEPARATE companies. It defines WHEN one entity must consolidate ANOTHER (the concept of CONTROL), and sets out the MECHANICS of combining, eliminating, and presenting the group's financial position and performance as a WHOLE.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s2">
  <span class="num">2</span>
  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cw span2">
    <div class="ctitle cw">Parent companies preparing group financial statements</div>
    <div class="principle">This Statement applies to ANY entity that is a PARENT — an entity CONTROLLING one or more OTHER entities (subsidiaries) — requiring the preparation of CONSOLIDATED financial statements presenting the GROUP as a single reporting entity.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s3">
  <span class="num">3</span>
  <h2>Defining Control — the Basis for Consolidation</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Majority voting rights, or de facto control indicators</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">CONTROL is generally PRESUMED where an entity holds a MAJORITY of another entity's VOTING rights. Where voting rights ALONE don't clearly establish control, J-GAAP ALSO considers "DE FACTO" control indicators — such as holding a SIGNIFICANT (though not majority) voting interest COMBINED WITH other factors demonstrating EFFECTIVE control (e.g. the ability to APPOINT a majority of the board, or CONTROLLING financial and operating POLICIES through contractual or other arrangements) — broadly PARALLELING IFRS 10's OWN control model internationally.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s4">
  <span class="num">4</span>
  <h2>Uniform Accounting Policies Within the Group</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cs span2">
    <div class="ctitle cs">Consistency across all consolidated entities</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">SUBSIDIARIES' financial statements must be prepared using UNIFORM accounting policies CONSISTENT with the parent's OWN policies for the purposes of consolidation — where a subsidiary applies a DIFFERENT policy in its OWN standalone reporting, adjustments must be made BEFORE consolidation, ensuring the CONSOLIDATED figures reflect a genuinely CONSISTENT basis of measurement throughout the group.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s5">
  <span class="num">5</span>
  <h2>Elimination of Intercompany Transactions and Balances</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Removing transactions that don't represent transactions with genuine outside parties</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">ALL intercompany transactions and BALANCES — sales, purchases, loans, dividends — between GROUP members are ELIMINATED on consolidation, ALONG WITH any UNREALISED profit remaining in inventory or other assets still HELD WITHIN the group — reflecting that, from the CONSOLIDATED group's perspective, these are NOT genuine transactions with OUTSIDE, unrelated parties.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s6">
  <span class="num">6</span>
  <h2>Non-Controlling Interests Presentation</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cw span2">
    <div class="ctitle cw">Presented as a distinct component within Net Assets</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">The portion of a SUBSIDIARY's net assets and profit/loss attributable to shareholders OTHER than the parent — NON-CONTROLLING INTERESTS (非支配株主持分) — is presented as a SEPARATE, distinct component WITHIN Net Assets (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 5 poster), and non-controlling interests' SHARE of profit/loss is presented SEPARATELY within the consolidated Statement of Income, distinguishing it from profit attributable to the PARENT's OWN shareholders (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 2, EPS, poster).</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s7">
  <span class="num">7</span>
  <h2>Fiscal Year-End Alignment — a Practical J-GAAP-Specific Rule</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Adjustments required where a subsidiary's year end differs materially</div>
    <div class="text-supporting">A DISTINCTIVE, PRACTICAL J-GAAP rule: where a SUBSIDIARY's fiscal year-end DIFFERS from the parent's by MORE than THREE MONTHS, the subsidiary must PREPARE financial statements as of a date CLOSER to the parent's own fiscal year-end (or the parent must otherwise make appropriate ADJUSTMENTS) for CONSOLIDATION purposes — ensuring the CONSOLIDATED figures reflect a genuinely COMPARABLE reporting period across the GROUP, rather than allowing a MATERIAL timing mismatch to persist unaddressed.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s8">
  <span class="num">8</span>
  <h2>Worked Example — Consolidating a Subsidiary at Acquisition</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cw span2">
    <div class="ctitle cw">Combining the subsidiary's assets/liabilities and recognising non-controlling interests</div>
    <div class="worked worked--flush">
      <div class="wk-title">Example: An 80%-owned subsidiary</div>
      <div class="wk-body">A parent acquires an 80% controlling interest in a subsidiary with identifiable net assets of ¥500,000,000 at fair value.</div>
      <div class="wk-answer">The parent CONSOLIDATES 100% of the subsidiary's assets and liabilities LINE-BY-LINE, and recognises NON-CONTROLLING INTERESTS of 20% × ¥500,000,000 =<strong>¥100,000,000</strong>WITHIN Net Assets — reflecting the PORTION of the subsidiary's net assets attributable to the OUTSIDE 20% shareholders, with GOODWILL calculated on the parent's OWN 80% acquired interest only (per the companion ASBJ Statement No. 21 poster's partial goodwill method).</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s9">
  <span class="num">9</span>
  <h2>Worked Example — Fiscal Year-End Misalignment</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card ci span2">
    <div class="ctitle ci">Adjusting for a subsidiary's differing year end</div>
    <div class="worked worked--flush">
      <div class="wk-title">Example: A subsidiary with a 6-month different fiscal year end</div>
      <div class="wk-body">A parent's fiscal year ends March 31. A foreign subsidiary's fiscal year ends September 30 — a 6-month difference, EXCEEDING the 3-month threshold.</div>
      <div class="wk-answer">The subsidiary must PREPARE additional financial statements as of a date CLOSER to March 31 (or the parent must make appropriate ADJUSTMENTS for significant intervening transactions) — the subsidiary CANNOT simply be consolidated using its September 30 figures UNADJUSTED, given the DIFFERENCE exceeds the 3-month threshold.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s10">
  <span class="num">10</span>
  <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 22 requires</div>
    <div class="check-list"><span>Basis for determining control and the scope of consolidation</span><span>List of significant consolidated subsidiaries</span><span>Non-controlling interests presentation and movement</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s11">
  <span class="num">11</span>
  <h2>Critical Judgments & Estimates</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cn span2">
    <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
        <div class="dot-list"><span>Whether de facto control exists absent majority voting rights</span><span>Whether a fiscal year-end difference requires adjustment</span></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
        <div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of a subsidiary's identifiable net assets at the date control is obtained</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s12">
  <span class="num">12</span>
  <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card ci span2">
    <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS 10</div>
    <div class="td-table">
      <div class="th cols-12-12-12"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 22)</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS (IFRS 10)</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-12-12-12"><span>Control definition</span><span>Majority voting rights, plus de facto control indicators</span><span>Power, exposure to variable returns, and the ability to affect those returns — converged in overall substance</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt cols-12-12-12"><span>Fiscal year-end alignment</span><span>Specific 3-month threshold rule</span><span>General requirement for consistent reporting dates, without the same specific numeric threshold</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="note">The OVERALL control-based consolidation MODEL is broadly CONVERGED with IFRS 10, reflecting SUBSTANTIAL mutual development during the 2000s convergence era — the MOST distinctive J-GAAP-specific feature is the SPECIFIC, numerically-defined fiscal year-end alignment rule.</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s13">
  <span class="num">13</span>
  <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cs span2">
    <div class="ctitle cs">Where every consolidation event lands</div>
    <div class="td-table">
      <div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Subsidiary consolidation</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Line-by-line combination, with intercompany eliminations</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt cols-16-1-14"><span>Non-controlling interests</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Presented separately within Net Assets and profit allocation</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s14">
  <span class="num">14</span>
  <h2>Related Standards</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cd span2">
    <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
    <div class="td-table">
      <div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
      <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 21</span><span>Business Combinations — supplies the goodwill and fair value measurement principles applied on initial consolidation</span></div>
      <div class="tr alt cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 5</span><span>Supplies the Net Assets presentation structure non-controlling interests are shown within</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="section-header" id="s15">
  <span class="num">15</span>
  <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
  <span class="line"></span>
</div>
<div class="grid">
  <div class="card cn span2">
    <div class="glossary-item">
      <div class="glossary-term">Control</div>
      <div class="glossary-def">The basis for consolidation, generally presumed at majority voting rights but also assessed through de facto control indicators.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="glossary-item glossary-item--last">
      <div class="glossary-term">De facto control</div>
      <div class="glossary-def">Effective control over an entity established through indicators other than majority voting rights, such as board appointment power or contractual arrangements.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="legend">
  <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
  <div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span>Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)<span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span>Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)<span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span>純資産の部<span class="badge be">SCNA</span>Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)<span class="badge bc">SCF</span>Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</div>
</div>
  </div>
</StandardPageLayout>
